From bd97042e1713c8d0a20201635f899c5efcb5d9f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HeDo <ldileo@digipa.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:33:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Nothing in the quadric simplification needs Eigen

The quadric simplification of a mesh without texture solved its 3x3 system with Eigen's
FullPivLU and its error with the Eigen norm. The solution is now computed by SolveFullPivot3x3,
plain code that does the same operations in the same order as Eigen's solver (the largest
remaining coefficient as pivot, the first one in column order winning a tie; the rank test with
3 * epsilon; the triangular systems by columns, a column of zero right-hand side skipped; the
unknowns no pivot reaches set to 0), so that the result is the same to the last bit, signs of
zeros included. It was compared with Eigen on 20 million quadrics, from planes in general
position, integer ones, coplanar ones, ones of every scale from 1e-160 to 1e160, and ones with
infinities and NaNs, with no difference.

What else of the files used here named Eigen is removed, because it cannot be compiled without
it and nothing in a triangle mesh pipeline calls it: Quadric::MinimumClosestToPoint (an SVD) and
the SVDPlacement option that chose it; Matrix33 and Matrix44 Inverse and the Eigen determinant
of Matrix44 (now a plain expansion by 2x2 minors); the Allocator::AddVertices and AddFaces that
take an Eigen matrix; the polygon functions that fit a plane or take the principal components of
a polygon or align a template to it (PolyFittingPlane, PolyFlatness, PolyPCA, PolyScaledPCA,
GetPolyTemplatePos, PolyAspectRatio); Stat::ComputeMeshVolume and Clean::SelectFoldedFaceFromOneRingFaces,
which called into them. With those gone, fitting3.h, point_matching.h and inertia.h are no
longer read.
